---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/content";
---

<Base title="About" description="About Ragib Badaruddin and this site.">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    I'm Ragib, a software engineer in Malaysia. Outside work, I build and run a
    few small, free things: a{" "}
    <a href="/projects/#bancuh-dns">public adblock DNS service</a> I started in
    2015, a <a href="/projects/#simplesolat">Muslim prayer times app</a>, an{" "}
    <a href="/projects/#gibtalk">AAC app</a> I first built for my own kids, and{" "}
    <a href="/projects/#keytree">keytree</a>, a small tool for managing SSH keys.
    Most of their websites and backends run on a{" "}
    <a href="/projects/#homelab">homelab</a> at home.
  </p>
  <p>
    They're small. But some people rely on them every day, and I learned early
    that you don't know who depends on something until you turn it off. So I try
    to keep them running, keep them free, and be honest about what they can and
    can't do.
  </p>
  <p>
    Most of what they taught me only lived in commit messages, old GitHub issues
    and a 2015 blog I had to rescue from the Wayback Machine. This site is where
    I write it down, in the order it happened: what I built, what went wrong,
    and what I'd do differently. Not advice, just notes.
  </p>
  <p>
    For my work history, see <a href={SITE.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>. For code, see{" "}
    <a href={SITE.github}>GitHub</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>This site</h2>
  <p>
    Built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> and served as static
    files from my homelab, deployed with Flux. No analytics, no cookies. The{" "}
    <a href={SITE.source}>source is on GitHub</a>. The writing is{" "}
    <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a> and the
    code is MIT.
  </p>
</Base>
